    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0781" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/494.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Brown to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Amapala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-04-24"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reports that the treaty of peace and amity which has been signed is similar to
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> treaty, and includes provision for a
                    Central American Peace Congress in Nicaragua and a special commercial treaty
                    between the two Republics. Adds that the friendly mediation of the United States
                    is gratefully acknowledged by both countries.</p>
            </div>
